# Line endings are LF in the repository and in the working tree, on every OS.
#
# Without this file, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true checks out CRLF,
# and then `gofmt -l .` flags every Go file while `go mod tidy -diff` reports
# go.sum drift — locally red, green in CI. A pre-release check that is wrong on
# the maintainer's own machine is worse than no check, because the habit it
# teaches is to ignore it.
#
# eol=lf (not just text=auto) is deliberate: text=auto alone still hands CRLF to
# the working tree under autocrlf, which is exactly the case that broke.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files whose tooling is line-ending sensitive.
*.go    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.rb    text eol=lf
go.mod  text eol=lf
go.sum  text eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.exe   binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip   binary
